# Each occupier's garrison (war window)
war-garrison-line = Garrison of { $by }: { $need } men needed; { $kept } kept, { $source }.
war-garrison-posts = all by garrison troops
war-garrison-field = all taken from the field army
war-garrison-mixed = { $posts } men of the garrison troops and { $field } taken from the field army
war-garrison-short = short of men
war-garrison-ordered = { $n } garrison men ordered.
war-garrison-tip = Each occupied region asks for a garrison that grows with its people and its resistance. Garrison troops stand first; what they miss comes out of the field army, up to half of it, and those men do not fight at the front. With the garrison short, resistance rises and the occupier takes less.
